  "decision_conditions": [
    "\r\n The proposed\r\n     development is unacceptable in principle, whereby the retention of shipping\r\n     containers and associated works would represent an uncharacteristic and\r\n     inharmonious development to the visual detriment of the character and\r\n     appearance of the immediate location resulting in an incompatible industrialised&nbsp;form\r\n     of development contrary to Policy 39 and 53 of the Waltham Forest adopted\r\n     Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).\r\n \r\n \r\n",
    "The existing restaurant use would have an adverse impact from noise and disturbance unduly compromising the amenity of local residents residing in the neighbouring and adjacent residential dwellings contrary to Policy 50 and 57 of the Waltham Forest adopted Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "The application failed to provide justification for Biodiversity net gain ‘below the threshold’ classification. In view of the absence of this information, an assessment could not be made whether the application should be classified as being below the threshold and therefore exempt from Biodiversity net gain in accordance with Schedule 7A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990."
  ],
